profile: mirust.workspace.current.v1
updated_utc: 2026-08-30T00:03:00Z
site: MiRust.com
status: ecosystem-governance-authority
current_authority:
  - Preserve Rust-first, local-first, checksum-bound engineering and evidence boundaries.
  - Treat TinyRustLM as one prelaunch clean-slate product with no legacy or compatibility obligation.
  - Read .uai/totem.uai and .uai/taboo.uai before changing ecosystem governance or claims.

memory_endpoints_two_lane_authority:
  direct_agent_coordination: Agents working on all ecosystem sites use MemoryEndpoints.com directly for agent-to-agent long-term memory, meetings, handoffs, and coordination.
  tinyrustlm_connect_user_plugin: Separately, the TinyRustLM.com Connect plugin lets a user sign in to MemoryEndpoints.com and explicitly select it as TinyRustLM.com Connect long-term memory.
  isolation: Keep lane identity, credentials, consent, scopes, provenance, idempotency, and receipts separate. Neither lane silently acts for the other.
  proof_boundary: Authorization, implementation, configuration, fixtures, mocks, or reachability do not prove live use, account correctness, synchronization, restore, deletion, cleanup, or continuity.

prelaunch_redundancy:
  policy: Important memory may also be kept in current .uai, wiki, public-safe source notes, and approved private stores for resilience.
  invariant: Every maintained copy stays current, secret-safe, provenance-labeled, and noncontradictory.
  conflict_rule: Surface and reconcile conflicts; do not silently choose one contradictory copy.

